{
  "meta": {
    "name": "Support Ticket Board",
    "tagline": "Live support pipeline as a Kanban — triage, work, escalate, and close tickets in one view.",
    "description": "Canonical Kanban example, modelled on the hs-uix demos. Compact card density (`cardDensity: 'compact'`) packs more tickets per column; `columnWidth: 320` keeps columns predictable across viewports; `countDisplay: 'tag'` shows per-stage counts as muted Tags in the headers. Body fields use `label` (description-list rows) instead of custom `$render` layouts — let the component own the layout, only reach for `$render` when you need a real custom cell (StatusTag for priority, Link for the title). Stage transitions use `stageControl: 'menu'` (transparent Dropdown) with `labels: { moveTo: 'Move' }` so the affordance stays out of the way until you reach for it. Top-of-board `metrics` surface the three numbers reps glance at; `recordLabel` controls the row-count + selection-bar copy. `selectable: true` + `selectionActions` is the bulk-action pattern — don't stuff bulk actions into per-card `KanbanCardActions`, those are for single-card moves. Search across multiple fields with `fuzzySearch`; multiselect filters for assignee + priority. Reach for this whenever a list of records flows through stages and reps need to see WIP at a glance.",
    "surface": "crm.record.tab",
    "object": "ticket"
  },
  "state": {},
